Z||000000||CUTTER||05-03-2000||11:26 AM||||I need a new starter and wanted to save some cash and put it in myself but need to know how hard it is and how long it will take. Where is the starter located?<BR>Thanks, Shane||||reg||1
Z||000001||Warhawk||05-03-2000||12:01 PM||||I just pulled the starter off my 4 cylinder Fiero.  Getting the starter off was quick and easy, but you have to pull the exhaust off to get to it, not so quick and easy. I'd say it took me an hour total to get the old starter off.  Probably a little longer to put it back on.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gokart||05-03-2000||08:47 PM||||Changed mine in my GT last fall. Don't remember the exhaust being in the way? Take a look at the shim before removing the original and try to get it back exactly where it was when you put in the new one. My son helped hold it up in place cause that sucker gets heavy after a while when your trying to line it up and get the bolts in. Get a partner if you can.||||reg||1
